{"key":"enterprise/T1548","id":"T1548","name":"Abuse Elevation Control Mechanism","domain":"enterprise","level":"technique","parent_id":null,"tactics":["privilege-escalation"],"platforms":["Linux","macOS","Windows","IaaS","Office Suite","Identity Provider"],"environments":["cloud","cloud-hosted-endpoint","identity","onprem"],"environment_basis":"project_taxonomy_from_upstream_platforms","summary":"Adversaries may circumvent mechanisms designed to control privilege elevation to gain higher-level permissions. Most modern systems contain native elevation control mechanisms that are intended to limit privileges that a user can perform on a machine. Authorization has to be granted to specific users in order to perform tasks that can be considered of higher risk. An adversary can perform several methods to take advantage of built-in control…","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1548","source_stix_id":"attack-pattern--67720091-eee3-4d2d-ae16-8264567f6f5b","source_modified":"2026-05-12T15:12:00.639Z","source_object_version":"2.0","telemetry":{"status":"mapped","components":[{"id":"DC0059","name":"File Metadata","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0059","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--639e87f3-acb6-448a-9645-258f20da4bc5","page":"telemetry/DC0059/"},{"id":"DC0088","name":"Logon Session Metadata","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0088","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--39b9db72-8b48-4595-a18d-db5bbba3091b","page":"telemetry/DC0088/"},{"id":"DC0021","name":"OS API Execution","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0021","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--9bde2f9d-a695-4344-bfac-f2dce13d121e","page":"telemetry/DC0021/"},{"id":"DC0032","name":"Process Creation","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0032","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--3d20385b-24ef-40e1-9f56-f39750379077","page":"telemetry/DC0032/"},{"id":"DC0034","name":"Process Metadata","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0034","stix_id":"x-mi